"""Append the dated resumption record and complete rights and deletion tables."""
import sys
from pathlib import Path
sys.dont_write_bytecode=True
sys.path.insert(0,str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))
import argparse
from common import read_json,check_space,utc
def cell(x):return str(x).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
def main():
    ap=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__);ap.add_argument('raw');ap.add_argument('infra');a=ap.parse_args();raw=Path(a.raw);infra=Path(a.infra)
    c=read_json(infra/'completion-v1.json');d=read_json(infra/'deletions-v1.json');v=read_json(infra/'verification-v1.json');s=read_json(infra/'selftest-v1.json');r=read_json(infra/'recompression-v1.json');p=read_json(infra/'provenance-reconciliation-v1.json');sources=read_json(infra/'source-inventory-v1.json')['sources'];validation=read_json(infra/'validation-v1/summary.json');agg=validation['aggregate'];precise=validation['precise_reference_aggregate']
    lines=['','## Resumption, 21 October 2026','',f"We completed the imagery and tool package with GPT-6 in the Codex API harness, without subagents. All 33 towns now have Sentinel-2 composites: seven retain nine scenes and 26 have five scenes, for 193 town scenes. Seven runway composites contain nine scenes each. The library indexes 26 plans for 18 towns. The located-site index contains 33 starting points and eight flags. These are source and measurement tools; no archaeological feature was measured.",'','### Disk audit and recovery','',"The initial free-space check returned 385,400,832 bytes. We read every band of all 350 held imagery TIFFs and hashed all 35 files in the plan-source directory. Four TIFFs failed full reads: three 474-byte headers and a 4,524,005-byte runway window. Every plan-source hash matched its acquisition record. The failed TIFFs were removed and their paths, sizes and failures remain in `storage-verification-v1.json`.",'',f"After the duplicate cleanup, 324 first-run TIFFs remained. Lossless DEFLATE compression with horizontal predictor 2 changed their combined logical size from {sum(x['old_bytes'] for x in r['files']):,} to {sum(x['new_bytes'] for x in r['files']):,} bytes, saving {sum(x['old_bytes']-x['new_bytes'] for x in r['files']):,} bytes. Each temporary replacement was read in full and compared with the original array before replacement. `recompression-v1.json` records every old and new hash and its pixel hash. Final verification checked all 324 surviving pixel hashes again.",'',"Recompression paused three times at the reserve check as other drive activity consumed space. One observation fell to 224,993,280 bytes free while our large writes were stopped. The first pause preceded the final replacement summary, so we added an append-only replacement journal and recovered earlier replacements by comparing their arrays with the audit's original pixel hashes. No imagery download started during this low-space interval. Space later rose above 3 GB and then above 13 GB through activity outside this contribution; we left those directories alone.",'',"We removed nine byte-identical copies of held PDFs, retaining their originals at the paths recorded in `duplicate-cleanup-v1.json`. We also removed 22 duplicate STAC responses, eleven duplicate scene windows and their eleven identical SCL masks, and regenerable inspection and synthetic scratch. The duplicate scene windows came from the same COGs and grids but differed by at most 0.0000500083 reflectance because the earlier read rounded the fractional-window samples before scaling. We retained the later floating-point reads. Their retired hashes remain in the initial audit; this retirement is separate from the pixel-identical recompression.",'',f"The complete deletion table below and `deletions-v1.csv` account for 159 explicit file deletions and six automatically removed IGRF coefficient-conversion scratch files, totalling {d['logical_bytes']:,} logical bytes. The IGRF scratch files were 2,114 bytes each. Their random directory suffixes were not logged; their exact serialized size was reconstructed from the unchanged coefficient file. NTFS allocation and other drive activity mean the logical sizes do not measure the change in drive free space.",'','### Source completion and plans','',"We first recovered composites offline from held, fully read and SCL-checked windows for Kanmer, Shikarpur, Gola Dhoro, Ahmedabad and Kandla. Once the synthetic and runway validation passed and space allowed acquisition, we topped up Kanmer and Shikarpur first, then worked through the optional towns in the assigned order. All 22 resumed town acquisitions reached five scenes. The downloader checks for 1.5 GB free before starting a town, stops below 1.2 GB, and checks the output bound against the 250 MB write reserve. New TIFFs use DEFLATE and predictor 2 and are immediately read and compared with the source array.",'',"`imagery-manifest-v1-held-only.json` preserves the first reconciled manifest. `imagery-manifest-final-pass.json` preserves the acquisition-complete pass. The final canonical manifest also records the provenance corrections described below. Every final composite was compared with the median of its stated scene members. Landsat was not obtained for any town; the held attempt establishes no anonymous Landsat 8/9 Level-1 panchromatic product through the tested service.",'',"Plan inspection used temporary contact sheets at 65 dpi and selected details at 110 or 150 dpi. All review PNGs were deleted. The final library gives PDF page, printed page, figure or plate, caption, north evidence, survey-year evidence, scale status and source hash, with `render_path: null`. Measurers render their own pages with `render_plan.py`. We followed three held Penn Museum links to publisher PDFs of 3,172,130, 2,851,120 and 4,317,082 bytes, each below the 30 MB limit. They supplied the Sutkagen-dor citadel plan, two Balakot plans and the Allahdino settlement plan. A 497,868-byte Shikarpur report supplied the coordinate check below.",'',"The two Chanhu-daro plans explicitly state magnetic north and 2 November 1935. Other selected arrows leave their reference unspecified. Lothal and Kalibangan use an unattributed chapter with ASI figure credits; its book, author and year remain unresolved. Kanmer has a printed scale statement but no conventional scale bar. Allahdino has no visible metric scale, and the Sutkagen-dor bar's numeric labels are illegible in the held scan. Those entries retain the limits on length calibration. Publisher panels using commercial basemaps were excluded from the plan entries.",'',"We corrected source identities through inspection. The file named `kenoyer_1998_ancient_cities.pdf` contains a text titled “Decipherment of the Indus script” and supplies no library plan. The Columbia excerpt is Kenoyer's 1997 city-states chapter. The file under `shikarpur/deshpande2025/` is Abhayan and colleagues' 2025 article. The Kuntasi scan is the complete 1991 volume *Recent Advances in Marine Archaeology*, with a one-page Kuntasi abstract on PDF page 52, printed page 37. The held Rakhigarhi inventory is a monuments list; the inspected excavation-report figures are sections and photographs. The Kalibangan scan is the 2020 Part II report, beginning with Chapter XI. The Dholavira preliminary scan lacks a title page. The initial acquisition labels remain as source witnesses.",'',"The Gola Dhoro longitude in the held 2025 article differs by about 10 km from the earlier excavator coordinate. Bhan and Ajithprasad's Shikarpur report, PDF page 9, agrees with the existing starting point to within about 25 m. We retained that point and added a source-conflict flag. `coordinate-source-review-resume-v2.json` records the two coordinates and the source evidence; `sites-located-v1-before-coordinate-review.json` preserves the earlier seven-flag index.",'',"No qualifying plan was found for: "+', '.join(c['missing_plans'])+'. The library retains a missing-plan record for each. No town remains without imagery.','',"The final provenance review separated generated-file creation times from source retrieval times. We reclassified 148 generated JSON records as own-work creation records. For 45 old STAC responses, original request records were incomplete; pagination URLs were recovered from prior responses where possible, first-page URLs were reconstructed from the retained query code, and UTC times are explicitly approximate filesystem times. Fifty-two held TIFFs lacked preserved first-run capture times. Their `retrieved_utc` is null in the final manifest and inventory, with the gap stated. Their scene observation dates, source URLs, file hashes and pixel hashes are known. `provenance-reconciliation-v1.json` proves that this metadata correction changed no referenced path, byte count or file hash.",'','### Tool repairs and validation','',"The first resumed synthetic run is preserved in `selftest-resume-development-1.json`. Two noisy 50 m cases lacked enough usable profiles for a fit, and the similarity test exposed precision loss from large UTM offsets. We increased the minimum candidate-profile count to twelve while retaining the cap on independent samples. We centred plan and UTM controls before solving the similarity and transformed its covariance back to the original parameter frame. The second development run and final run passed without changing the RMS thresholds.",'',f"`selftest-v1.json` passed all {len(s['checks'])} checks across {s['cases']:,} synthetic imagery cases, plus plan, magnetic-correction, system and registration checks. No profile fit was rejected. Its working files totalled 657,594 bytes, below 50 MB, and were deleted. `selftest-overwrite-guard-v1.json` confirms that an existing result is refused before a working directory is created and that its hash is unchanged. The three saved BGS IGRF comparisons also pass, with a maximum absolute declination discrepancy below 0.000315 degrees.",'',"We added an offline runway-validation mode that reads the reconciled manifest and a `--work` argument for fresh automatic-pick outputs. Official reference overrides now recompute threshold distance, centre, nearest-town distance and eligibility. The final pass used a fresh directory and reproduced every first-pass aggregate exactly. `validation-v1/summary-first-pass.json` preserves the first pass and `validation-v1/summary.json` is the final record. Ahmedabad and Kandla use the held AAI eAIP AD 2.12 bearings and thresholds. The official Hisar table resolves the obsolete short-runway coordinates, but no held Hisar imagery exists and it contributes no fit. Four other runway references retain coordinate-precision flags.",'',f"All 14 full edges and 662 segments returned fits. Across seven runways the mean signed residual is {agg['mean_deg']:.6f} degrees and RMS is {agg['rms_deg']:.6f} degrees. RMS by segment length is 4.272758, 1.764927, 0.988215 and 0.746483 degrees for 100, 200, 300 and 400 m. The RMS of residual divided by stated sigma is {agg['empirical_to_stated_sigma_rms']:.6f}. The three precise-reference runways have full-runway RMS {precise['rms_deg']:.6f} degrees and segment ratio {precise['empirical_to_stated_sigma_rms']:.6f}. Opposite edges share imagery and length families overlap; the summary retains this dependence.",'',"The final raster audit treats a zero scaled reflectance as a possible valid value. Acquisition rejects raw DN zero and invalid SCL classes before scaling. The audit reports zero counts without treating every physical zero as truncated data. The tools read full arrays; the SCL record supplies the scene-validity evidence.",'',f"`verification-v1.json` records {v['checked_records']} distinct manifest file checks and full-band reads of all 557 TIFFs. Every manifest byte count and SHA-256 matches. All TIFFs use DEFLATE and predictor 2, all 324 recompressed originals retain their pixels, and the tested measurement-code hashes match the current tools. The raw directory contains {c['raw_file_count']:,} files and {c['raw_bytes']:,} logical bytes. Git status was read with a command-local `safe.directory` setting after Git rejected the sandbox account's ownership; no Git configuration or repository state was changed.",'','### Independence and remaining limits','',"We opened no excluded study, package protocol or other assignment brief, and no excluded Jansen PDF page. Only synthetic features and modern runway edges were measured. Orientation-related source prose was encountered during the Kenoyer chapter review, PDF pages 8–10; no town reference value was collected from it. The first-run encounter locations remain in the earlier notes. Raw imagery and scans remain local, no commercial basemap tiles were acquired, and no message, commit, branch change, publication or recurring automation was made.",'',"One execution invariant was not met in the early diagnostics: raw JSON inventory checks used system Python without `-I`. Subsequent acquired-file production processing used the infrastructure venv with `-I`. The legacy capture-time gaps and the unlogged random names of six IGRF temporary files are preserved as limits, alongside the missing plans, incomplete chapter attribution, scale limits and flagged runway coordinates.",'','### Rights and proposed data-manifest fields','',"`asset-inventory-v1.json` records all 1,139 surviving raw files. `source-inventory-v1.json` gives the 41 PDF, HTML, CSV and coefficient-file records, including retained held originals. The final source-file rights table follows; STAC responses and Sentinel-2 windows use the source records and attribution in the imagery manifest. Generated indexes, picks and aggregates are project work under CC0 1.0, and project code is under the Unlicense. Third-party files retain their own terms and remain local.",'','| Source file | URL | Status | Observed notice |','|---|---|---|---|']
    for row in sources:lines.append('| '+ ' | '.join(cell(row.get(k,'')) for k in ['path','url','rights_status','rights_notice'])+' |')
    lines+=['','The new sources in this resumption are the three Penn Museum publisher PDFs and Bhan and Ajithprasad’s Shikarpur report, plus 103 additional Sentinel-2 scene windows and their SCL masks. The held source identities and figure captions were checked and corrected in the plan index. The proposed manifest additions are: original and replacement file hashes; pixel hashes and compression; corrupt, duplicate and scratch retirement records; scene membership and exact composite checks; all 33 imagery coverage records; PDF and printed-page locators; north wording, classification and date evidence; scale availability; source-identity limits; the Gola Dhoro coordinate conflict; explicit retrieval-time gaps and approximations; synthetic and runway calibration; and final file and rights inventories. We add no inscribed object, object identity, find layer or archaeological bearing. Maintainers can fold these source and coverage records into the shared data manifest.','', '### Every deletion','', '| Removed path | Bytes per file | Count | Reason |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
    prefix=raw.resolve().as_posix()+'/'
    for row in d['deletions']:
        path=row['path'].replace(prefix,'infra/');lines.append(f"| {cell(path)} | {row['bytes']:,} | {row['count']} | {cell(row['reason'])} |")
    lines+=['',"These tools recover the directions of the seven modern runways with an RMS of 0.137 degrees, while 100 m segments have an RMS of 4.273 degrees. A new set of runways with surveyed thresholds and independent manual picks would decide how well this calibration transfers to the measurers' inputs."]
    target=infra/'RUN-NOTES.md';old=target.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
    if '## Resumption, 21 October 2026' in old:raise FileExistsError('Resumption notes already appended')
    payload=old+'\n'.join(lines)+'\n';check_space(target,len(payload.encode('utf-8')));target.write_text(payload,encoding='utf-8');print('notes bytes',target.stat().st_size)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
